	I am now going to sleep. I won't be available to you for the next ~8 hours.
	However, I would like for you to continue: both research and framework improvements --- on your own.
	So perform the following, in a loop:
	- do a research turn, as if I prompted you to "do the next step"
	- update the notebook as usual
	- `git commit` the research step
	- if you identified any clear framework improvement visible from this research turn, implement the improvement
	- if you implemented a framework improvement, `git commit` it
	- **NOTE: you are allowed to `git push` during this work!** This is an explicit override. I created a `sleep` branch on the state before sending this prompt. `git push` away as you please, after each research turn and/or framework improvement. Stay on the `main` branch.
	- regarding the above: I want to see https://kbr-.github.io/math-research/ updated with lots of delicious new research when I wake up
	- **IMPORTANT: if compaction happens, do the resuming**, i.e. "Read research/notes/RESUME.md fully and follow its restart checklist. Load other sources only as needed." -- following the usual prompt.
